WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.075
- You have to surround
yourself with people that are

00:00:02.075 --> 00:00:05.360
going to move you higher, as Oprah said,

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.371
or somebody said.

00:00:06.371 --> 00:00:09.704
(relaxed hip hop music)

00:00:11.071 --> 00:00:12.072
- I was like 10.

00:00:12.072 --> 00:00:13.312
I was with my dad at his office.

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.079
I was like on one of the
intern's computers or something,

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:16.746
and I'm thinking to my 10 year old self,

00:00:16.746 --> 00:00:18.478
"Hey, I wanna look up boys.com.

00:00:18.478 --> 00:00:20.813
"I'm sure it's gonna be
full of fire trucks."

00:00:20.813 --> 00:00:22.748
It wasn't (chuckles).

00:00:22.748 --> 00:00:25.501
That's when I first started
feeling this attraction to it.

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:29.788
My mom caught me a year or two after that,

00:00:29.788 --> 00:00:31.455
and she flipped out.

00:00:32.587 --> 00:00:35.183
I kinda saw how my mom reacted
to how other black people

00:00:35.183 --> 00:00:39.843
would react, especially how
I thought my dad would react.

00:00:39.843 --> 00:00:43.024
- I thought I had my shit all
hidden, folder after folder

00:00:43.024 --> 00:00:47.191
after folder, and my brother
happened to find some clips,

00:00:48.293 --> 00:00:51.720
and then he called it out in
front of my mom (chuckles).

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.667
And I was mortified.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:55.840
And I mean, I guess the
writing is on the damn wall

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:56.921
at that point.

00:00:56.921 --> 00:00:58.848
I was just like, "Well, here I am.

00:00:58.848 --> 00:01:00.252
"I'm gay.

00:01:00.252 --> 00:01:01.495
"Now do you have a problem
with it, and if you do,

00:01:01.495 --> 00:01:03.035
"I don't care."

00:01:03.035 --> 00:01:04.514
- Well when someone tells
you you're something,

00:01:04.514 --> 00:01:06.673
and you cancel it out, you don't listen,

00:01:06.673 --> 00:01:08.415
and you're like, "Nope, nope,"
and then there was a moment

00:01:08.415 --> 00:01:11.167
I was 15, I was like, "Wait, am I gay?"

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:15.180
And my heart sunk because
I knew what that meant,

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.097
and it was hard, you
know, just that feeling of

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:22.705
being scared to just be yourself.

00:01:22.705 --> 00:01:23.947
No one should have to go through that.

00:01:23.947 --> 00:01:27.588
- My parents were super,
super, super strict Catholics.

00:01:27.588 --> 00:01:30.577
I went through the whole,
we called it religion class.

00:01:30.577 --> 00:01:34.114
Very traditional, and it
was always talking about

00:01:34.114 --> 00:01:37.693
man and woman, and I'm just
like, "What, huh, who?"

00:01:37.693 --> 00:01:41.068
- I was also a minority
in terms of my religion

00:01:41.068 --> 00:01:42.590
that I grew up in.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.764
Maybe the only black family
in the church, you know,

00:01:44.764 --> 00:01:47.328
but the Mormon religion
is so misunderstood

00:01:47.328 --> 00:01:50.185
because I can tell you
without a shadow of a doubt

00:01:50.185 --> 00:01:54.352
that I never once felt
bullied or like I wasn't seen.

00:01:55.596 --> 00:01:58.290
- The church that I grew up
on was totally apolitical.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.744
I didn't really feel that
kind of homophobia that does

00:02:01.744 --> 00:02:06.091
happen in the black church until
my family switched churches

00:02:06.091 --> 00:02:07.438
while I was away.

00:02:07.438 --> 00:02:08.791
I'm there in the service and they're like,

00:02:08.791 --> 00:02:10.673
"We're gonna sign this
petition after service

00:02:10.673 --> 00:02:13.229
"and let them know that we
don't accept this gay marriage,"

00:02:13.229 --> 00:02:16.159
whatever, whatever, and
I'm like, "Okay, no, stop."

00:02:16.159 --> 00:02:17.703
And my dad's like, "Warren,
why are you so upset?"

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:19.886
And I'm like, "Because
I think I'm gay, Dad."

00:02:19.886 --> 00:02:21.163
And he just looks at me and he's like,

00:02:21.163 --> 00:02:22.672
"Well, I mean he didn't have a
girlfriend all of high school

00:02:22.672 --> 00:02:23.775
"and that's stupid."

00:02:23.775 --> 00:02:26.105
- Masculinity in my home was
expressed through sports,

00:02:26.105 --> 00:02:28.814
and I started flipping
off shit and I ended up

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:31.821
getting into gymnastics
because I wanted to be like

00:02:31.821 --> 00:02:34.760
Dominique Dawes and my
parents supported it.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.873
They still support my crazy dreams.

00:02:36.873 --> 00:02:38.137
I was a damn good athlete.

00:02:38.137 --> 00:02:42.109
People think because I'm
feminine that I can't beat you

00:02:42.109 --> 00:02:46.276
in a track race, but I grew
up very lucky to have a family

00:02:48.657 --> 00:02:52.657
that focused on my talents
and my skills and not

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:55.832
what they didn't understand.

00:02:55.832 --> 00:02:57.609
- So far as like black gay characters

00:02:57.609 --> 00:03:01.412
or black female characters,
like I didn't really see

00:03:01.412 --> 00:03:02.500
much of myself.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.706
Especially like back
then, they were always

00:03:04.706 --> 00:03:06.166
so stereotypical.

00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:09.396
I will say though, when
I saw Rent, Collins,

00:03:09.396 --> 00:03:13.176
Jesse L. Martin's character
who's like this out,

00:03:13.176 --> 00:03:16.850
proud HIV positive gay
man, it's the first kind of

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.598
breaking up that stereotype.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.516
Like I kinda saw a little
bit of myself there.

00:03:20.516 --> 00:03:23.347
And the fact that he was
dating this awesome drag queen,

00:03:23.347 --> 00:03:26.262
like, this is very cool,
and that was kind of

00:03:26.262 --> 00:03:30.429
the first time I saw myself
so completely in a character.

00:03:31.986 --> 00:03:35.182
- Kerry Washington, when she
was falling into those roles

00:03:35.182 --> 00:03:38.084
where they wanted her
to be that ghetto girl

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.174
and she killed it and that
inspired me to embrace

00:03:40.174 --> 00:03:41.257
my blackness.

00:03:42.194 --> 00:03:45.516
Now she's doing Scandal and
that inspired me to know that

00:03:45.516 --> 00:03:48.626
I am powerful beyond belief.

00:03:48.626 --> 00:03:52.086
You can go from the streets of
Brooklyn to the White House.

00:03:52.086 --> 00:03:56.253
- Growing up, I used to run
home every day and watch Oprah.

00:03:57.206 --> 00:03:59.352
To this day, this woman has
probably inspired so many

00:03:59.352 --> 00:04:03.231
black people, white people,
queer people, straight people,

00:04:03.231 --> 00:04:04.497
everybody.

00:04:04.497 --> 00:04:08.433
She really had that voice of
reason that I looked up to

00:04:08.433 --> 00:04:09.555
every day.

00:04:09.555 --> 00:04:11.870
- The hardest part at least
for me was figuring out

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:13.957
how I could be like
confident in my blackness

00:04:13.957 --> 00:04:16.257
and confident in my homosexuality.

00:04:16.257 --> 00:04:20.100
So often, there's so much
negativity from one of those

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.413
to the other.

00:04:21.413 --> 00:04:24.780
- I have learned to really invest in

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.277
really good friendships.

00:04:26.277 --> 00:04:29.396
The journey I think is
finding people outside of

00:04:29.396 --> 00:04:31.126
your family.

00:04:31.126 --> 00:04:35.647
- I was like, "Dad, this
person said that I'm this,

00:04:35.647 --> 00:04:38.339
"and I can't even tell
my family that I'm gay."

00:04:38.339 --> 00:04:40.453
He said, "The only thing
that gets me mad is that

00:04:40.453 --> 00:04:42.403
"you waited so long to tell me."

00:04:42.403 --> 00:04:44.293
I mean, I'm still emotional
about it too because

00:04:44.293 --> 00:04:46.043
we don't speak on it.

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:51.088
- I wish that I could see
ahead of time and see that

00:04:51.088 --> 00:04:53.062
it isn't gonna be that bad.

00:04:53.062 --> 00:04:55.043
- The world is infinite.

00:04:55.043 --> 00:04:58.038
The possibilities are endless,
and there are a billion

00:04:58.038 --> 00:05:02.205
different paths for you
bigger than you liking men,

00:05:03.704 --> 00:05:05.937
or bigger than you having dark skin.

00:05:05.937 --> 00:05:08.538
Those two things are
things to be so proud of.

00:05:08.538 --> 00:05:12.214
- The black community has
a don't ask, don't tell

00:05:12.214 --> 00:05:13.971
type policy.

00:05:13.971 --> 00:05:17.523
It's okay to speak on it, and when you do,

00:05:17.523 --> 00:05:20.994
you can have a beautiful
relationship of love and support.

00:05:20.994 --> 00:05:24.885
Love in the black community
needs to be highlighted

00:05:24.885 --> 00:05:26.719
and expressed.

00:05:26.719 --> 00:05:28.159
- You're gonna go to
school, you're gonna learn,

00:05:28.159 --> 00:05:30.282
and then you're gonna get a bomb ass job,

00:05:30.282 --> 00:05:32.245
and you're gonna build your
career and you're gonna be

00:05:32.245 --> 00:05:33.250
fucking great.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.985
You can do it.

00:05:34.985 --> 00:05:35.920
Now go do it.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.677
Make us all proud.

00:05:37.677 --> 00:05:41.010
(relaxed hip hop music)

